{
  "selected_feature_id": 17,
  "rationale": "Sex is a well-established, biologically grounded predictor of hypertension risk that should remain predictive across BRFSS domains and adds complementary signal beyond age, diabetes, physical activity, and cost barriers. It is more stable and less domain-identifying than state or year, and less likely to act as a brittle socioeconomic or demographic shortcut than race, employment, or poverty."
}

